<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v2.3 20070202//EN" "archivearticle.dtd"><article xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" article-type="review-article"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="pmc">comsigrev</journal-id><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">COMSIG Rev</journal-id><journal-title>COMSIG review</journal-title><publisher><publisher-name>Chiropractors &#x00026; Osteopaths Musculo-Skeletal Interest Group</publisher-name></publisher></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmid">17989764</article-id><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">2062509</article-id><article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Article</subject></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title>Type &#x0201c;O&#x0201d; Disorders</article-title><subtitle>President's Report</subtitle></title-group><contrib-group><contrib contrib-type="author"><name><surname>Walker</surname><given-names>Bruce F.</given-names></name><degrees>D.C.</degrees></contrib></contrib-group><pub-date pub-type="ppub"><day>1</day><month>7</month><year>1993</year></pub-date><volume>2</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>29</fpage><lpage>30</lpage><copyright-statement>Chiropractic &#x00026; Osteopathic College of Australasia</copyright-statement><copyright-year>1993</copyright-year><abstract><p>In this issue of the Review we publish our policy on the subject of chiropractic or osteopathic treatment of visceral disease, the so-called type "O" disorders</p><p>It is time that both the professions make an unambiguous statement on this controversial subject.  Anecdotal references and old philosophical cliches are not enough any more. Instead we need a more rational, logical and ethical approach to the problem.  This should where possible be based on scientifically conducted research.</p></abstract><kwd-group><kwd>Type "O"</kwd><kwd>visceral disorders</kwd><kwd>evidence based practice</kwd><kwd>chiropractic</kwd></kwd-group></article-meta></front></article>